      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Management of childhood craniopharyngioma remains controversial. Aggressive primary surgery is associated with an increased risk of severe obesity, but hypothalamus-sparing surgery might increase the need for reoperation and/or irradiation. Nevertheless, hypothalamus-sparing strategies decreased occurrence of obesity\u2014a risk factor for impaired quality of life\u2014without increasing recurrence rates in a new study."},
